      "content": "The argument that free trade has gutted manufacturing is a common talking point, but it ignores the fact that globalization also created massive wealth and new industries in the West. While protectionism might temporarily shield some specific jobs, it does so by raising consumer costs and stifling innovation across the entire economy. True national efficiency comes from a dynamic, competitive market, not from insulating industries from global realities.",
